(7632163, 1237151, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done, Anita! I was one of the 10''s. These phones are incredible... As for "Easter Eggs", those are when a creator hides an element somewhere for you (the viewer) to discover: like that tiny person at the far left. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/> Thanks for the explanation, not sure if us Aussies down under use that term. Never heard it before. Anyway you are hundred percent correct about this phone, I travelled with two other cameras, but I used this phone camera probably even more so, very convenient and so light of course. And of course thank you for the 10 :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: Well done, Anita! I was one of the 10''s. These phones are incredible... As for "Easter Eggs", those are when a creator hides an element somewhere for you (the viewer) to discover: like that tiny person at the far left.    Thanks for the explanation, not sure if us Aussies down under use that term. Never heard it before. Anyway you are hundred percent correct about this phone, I travelled with two other cameras, but I used this phone camera probably even more so, very convenient and so light of course. And of course thank you for the 10 :-)', '2019-06-07 01:15:08.000000', NULL, 0),
